            {
                "entry_id": "563ea531-b202-3a5d-b221-0cc36f4bc8d1",
                "word": "pharisaism",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "b20628de-86b2-4b56-8f9e-d47cf1610976",
                        "entry_id": "563ea531-b202-3a5d-b221-0cc36f4bc8d1",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "pharisaisms"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "d0781a89-bfaf-35df-be0e-2b7feab79ebb",
                        "entry_id": "563ea531-b202-3a5d-b221-0cc36f4bc8d1",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The doctrines and practices, or the character and spirit, of the Pharisees."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "countable",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "b86aae5c-595c-40cf-8b77-5a986e60c05e",
                                "sense_id": "d0781a89-bfaf-35df-be0e-2b7feab79ebb",
                                "text": "Since Paul lived and worked in the greater Syrian area as a Pharisee, it is somewhat probable that Pharisaism had some influence there and that some Pharisees lived outside Jerusalem and Judea. […] Paul never says where he made contact with Pharisaism, in Tarsus, Syria, or Jerusalem. […] The evidence concerning Pharisaism is so slim that we do not know how Paul came to know about Pharisaism, why he was attracted to it, and what being a Pharisee entailed."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "761423bb-f7b9-4b0b-abc1-065125154d92",
                                "sense_id": "d0781a89-bfaf-35df-be0e-2b7feab79ebb",
                                "text": "Serious and substantial doubts about Paul's former life as a Pharisee, or even any contact with pharisaism on his part, have been raised."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "8cd7aae3-80c8-3bcc-8a8e-d045aa074e8f",
                        "entry_id": "563ea531-b202-3a5d-b221-0cc36f4bc8d1",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Rigid observance of external forms of religion without genuine piety; hypocrisy in religion; a censorious, self-righteous spirit in matters of morals or manners."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "countable",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "cd6d0c4b-a0b8-493f-b24d-1c45c1a3d802",
                                "sense_id": "8cd7aae3-80c8-3bcc-8a8e-d045aa074e8f",
                                "text": "[T]he Phariſee faſted twice every weeke, and that never cenſured in him as a peice of Phariſaiſme, or hypocriſie, or fault of any kind; but as commendable, if he had not boaſted of it."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "7c7a4667-cbec-4e56-9616-202cbf7a4df9",
                                "sense_id": "8cd7aae3-80c8-3bcc-8a8e-d045aa074e8f",
                                "text": "But denunciations do not go far, and the only living and effective protest would be a society itself delivered from all pharisaisms and idolatries."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "985869fe-b84b-4dc9-ac1f-7d3827ed2ee8",
                                "sense_id": "8cd7aae3-80c8-3bcc-8a8e-d045aa074e8f",
                                "text": "The codes of some modern pharisaism comprise mostly some virtues and moral rules selected from the codes of the Christian pharisaisms which they oppose […]"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "d31661e4-7e12-46e1-a149-01214ce2075a",
                        "source_entry_id": "563ea531-b202-3a5d-b221-0cc36f4bc8d1",
                        "source_sense_description": "doctrines and practices of the Pharisees",
                        "target_lang_word": "pharisaïsme",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "pharisaïsme",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a73e050d-52de-390e-810e-c208d4a0fd68",
                                        "entry_id": "34c4653b-fdfb-383a-be57-83638ce50ad8",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Doctrine, attitude des pharisiens, qui consiste à surveiller uniquement le respect de la loi (les actes), sans tenir compte de son esprit (l'intention, le but)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "04af7681-f2f8-4c45-9a36-05fb95d7abf0",
                                                "sense_id": "a73e050d-52de-390e-810e-c208d4a0fd68",
                                                "text": "Demandons donc à Dieu de nous purifier du pharisaïsme des oeuvres, de la comptabilité de nos mérites, du souci de notre perfection et de notre salut afin que nous n'ayons qu'une préoccupation : celle de ne jamais blesser Son Amour et de laisser Sa Vie s'exprimer dans la nôtre."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "550f609f-933d-3a43-8f66-84c575d6b84b",
                                        "entry_id": "34c4653b-fdfb-383a-be57-83638ce50ad8",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Piété ostentatoire ; hypocrisie en religion."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7d319682-68f8-4946-880f-de4fdff1e828",
                                                "sense_id": "550f609f-933d-3a43-8f66-84c575d6b84b",
                                                "text": "Si les moralités dont nous avons parlé n’ont pas été un frein pour le débordement des puissants, si elles ont aggravé seulement le pharisaïsme de leurs mœurs en nécessitant qu’un voile d’hypocrisie fût jeté sur le mystère de leurs alcôves, combien n’ont-elles point causé de désespoirs, de douleurs inutiles, de remords absurdes, de perversions, de suicides et de crimes chez les faibles et les sincères […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e60e4843-9e4f-4862-9065-47ecd74462be",
                                                "sense_id": "550f609f-933d-3a43-8f66-84c575d6b84b",
                                                "text": "Ah ! le temps joyeux de la stupidité, du pharisaïsme à rebours où les petits messieurs pressés se hissaient paisiblement sur la crête de la notoriété. Tous des faiseurs, tous des faisans."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "905c7a5b-d90b-4958-b34f-5e39e6e09e83",
                                                "sense_id": "550f609f-933d-3a43-8f66-84c575d6b84b",
                                                "text": "Elle blâmait encore le pharisaïsme de son milieu, mais sans condamner toute l’humanité."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "29ce1272-6415-3cd8-8f62-dfa55f74f6ad",
                                        "entry_id": "34c4653b-fdfb-383a-be57-83638ce50ad8",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Vertu ostentatoire ; comportement utilisé pour se décrire publiquement comme une personne ou une organisation vertueuse."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "broadly"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1532c91d-363b-4ed0-a7ac-63c9f12f0437",
                                                "sense_id": "29ce1272-6415-3cd8-8f62-dfa55f74f6ad",
                                                "text": "Certains voient dans le politiquement correct un pharisaïsme moderne."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
